# USS is not full CSS (UI Toolkit)

USS **looks** like CSS but is a **Unity subset**. Do not paste web/CSS snippets and assume they compile or layout correctly.

**Authority:** [USS supported properties (Unity 6)](https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.4/Documentation/Manual/UIE-USS-SupportedProperties.html), [USS selectors](https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.4/Documentation/Manual/UIE-USS-Selectors.html), [USS pseudo-classes](https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.4/Documentation/Manual/UIE-USS-Selectors-Pseudo-Classes.html). When unsure, check the manual — not MDN.

## Common traps (not in USS or not like the web)

| Web CSS habit | USS reality |
|---------------|-------------|
| `calc(100% - 24px)` | **No `calc()`** — use fixed px, theme `var(--token)`, flex grow/shrink, or C# |
| `min()` / `max()` / `clamp()` | **Not supported** — discrete BEM modifiers or C# |
| CSS Grid (`display: grid`) | **Flexbox only** — `display: flex` / default flex children |
| `@media (max-width: …)` | **No responsive `@media`** — BEM modifiers toggled in C#, separate layout classes, or `UIDocument` / panel settings |
| `:first-child`, `:last-child`, `:nth-child()` | **Not supported** — rules silently no-op; use BEM segment modifiers from C# (`--segment-start` / `--segment-mid` / `--segment-end`) or `ToggleButtonGroup` left/mid/right classes |
| Complex selectors (`:not()`, `+`, `~`, deep chains) | **Limited** — prefer one BEM class per node; shallow selectors |
| `::before` / `::after` content | **Limited / not for arbitrary content** — use extra `VisualElement` in UXML |
| Orchestrated show/hide motion | **Do not rely on USS `transition-*` alone** — `UiToolkitTweens` + ADR 039 (`unity-ui-toolkit.mdc`) |
| Layout from runtime geometry (markers, world bounds) | **C# inline `style`** or tween — USS cannot know coordinates ahead of time |

## What USS does support (use these)

- Flex layout (`flex-direction`, `flex-grow`, `align-items`, `justify-content`, …)
- Theme variables: `var(--spacing-md)`, `var(--color-*)` from project Theme StyleSheet
- BEM class selectors; state pseudo-classes only (`:hover`, `:active`, `:focus`, `:enabled`, `:disabled`, `:checked`, `:root` — see [pseudo-classes](https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.4/Documentation/Manual/UIE-USS-Selectors-Pseudo-Classes.html))
- Fixed units: `px`, `%`, and supported keywords (`auto`, `none`, … per manual)

## When math or responsiveness is needed

| Need | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Rail offset beside command rail | Fixed px in USS (e.g. `left: 240px`) + modifier class — see `centralized-ui-services.mdc` |
| Few discrete sizes | Mutually exclusive BEM modifiers (`map-view--panel-cell-24`) — C# picks one |
| Value depends on measured layout | C# sets `style.left` / `style.width` once per layout pass — not USS `calc` |
| Hide/show steady state | BEM `--hidden` / `--collapsed` — motion in C# tweens |
| Segmented tab / chip end caps | C# adds `--segment-start` / `--segment-end` on build (`RailMenuView.SetItems`) — not `:first-child` / `:last-child` |

## Examples

```css
/* ❌ BAD — calc does not exist in USS */
.command-rail__panel {
    width: calc(100% - var(--rail-width));
}

/* ✅ GOOD — token or fixed layout */
.command-rail__panel {
    flex-grow: 1;
    margin-left: 240px;
}
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD — assumes web media queries */
@media (max-width: 1280px) {
    .hub-hud { display: none; }
}

/* ✅ GOOD — C# toggles hub-hud--compact on root */
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD — structural pseudo-classes are not in USS; selector never matches */
.tabbed-picker__tabs .rail-menu__item:first-child {
    border-top-left-radius: 12px;
}

/* ✅ GOOD — segment modifier toggled in C# when tab buttons are built */
.rail-menu__item--segment-start {
    border-top-left-radius: 13px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 13px;
}
```

## Agent / PR checklist

- [ ] New USS property verified in [supported properties](https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.4/Documentation/Manual/UIE-USS-SupportedProperties.html)
- [ ] No `calc` / `clamp` / grid / `@media` without explicit team exception
- [ ] No `:first-child`, `:last-child`, `:nth-child` — use BEM modifiers or `ToggleButtonGroup` segment classes
- [ ] Dynamic layout → C# or discrete modifiers, not web-only CSS
